        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amélie Mauresmo, Pam Shriver, Loïc Courteau, Betsy Nagelsen\n- Events: 1985 Edgbaston Cup – Singles\n- Roles: tennis player, coach\n\nFacts:\n- Pam Shriver was the defending champion and won the 1985 Edgbaston Cup singles final by defeating Betsy Nagelsen 6–1, 6–0.\n- Pam Shriver, born on July 4, 1962, is an American former professional tennis player known primarily as a doubles specialist who also had success in singles.\n- Amélie Mauresmo, born on 5 July 1979, is a French former professional tennis player and a former world No. 1.\n- Since 2002, Loïc Courteau has coached Amélie Mauresmo, who won two Grand Slam titles.\n- Loïc Courteau has also coached the French Fed Cup team in past years.",
